      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_93b510b1e1811be76d1ee65b0480f23bfc0f427d344b1fc2ce4b90377a9a6524",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "Zero-spacing correlations motivate comparison of L-function zeros with random-matrix eigenvalue statistics, organizing conjectured family behavior by orthogonal, unitary, or symplectic symmetry classes. Compatibility with the Hilbert-Polya idea makes a self-adjoint spectral model plausible as an explanation of real spectral parameters, while the finite-field theory supplies an unconditional comparison setting rather than a classical operator.",
