    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_3dd61522d341f9a08eddc200898cabb8e77b06b7ba8eb5ec6d8b0aa1fb716f8f",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The finite-field geometric route and the spectral-statistical route supply complementary functional clues. In the geometric case, a divisor intersection pairing and the algebraic index theorem make the required negativity structural; in the spectral analogy, universal spacing comparisons are compatible with real spectral parameters arising from a self-adjoint operator. The classical gap is not filled by either clue: the survey explicitly asks for global counterparts of cohomology, Frobenius, and an index theorem, and supplies neither a classical pairing nor the conjectured operator.",
